#795 IS THE INVERTED CASE AGAIN (like #688 last time, d4831b93 before that): a
GUI-VISIBLE break fixed in a SHARED module. SWIG 4.5.0 deleted
`SwigPyIterator.next()`, which KiCad's OWN hand-written `__iter__` for TRACKS /
DRAWINGS / VECTOR_SHAPEPTR calls, so `build_pcb_data_from_board` could not read
a board at all on an Arch-built KiCad. The shim (py_router/swig_compat.py) is
called from kicad_parser (covers every shipped module that walks a board),
kicad_exact_fill (its refill SUBPROCESS imports that module, not the parser) AND
action_plugin (the GUI entry, before _get_selected_net_names walks a board) --
so BOTH fronts are repaired at the same import-time seam. Parity direction:
both-fronts-broken, shared-module-fix. Its gate asserts the GUI entry
BEHAVIOURALLY (import action_plugin against a deliberately broken fake pcbnew,
require the process to come back repaired) rather than grepping for the call.

